# BUPATI WONOSOBO REGULATION
NUMBER 45 OF 2011

CONCERNING

PROCEDURES FOR GRANTING PERMITS AND NON-PERMIT SERVICES
IN THE INTEGRATED LICENSING SERVICE OFFICE

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

BUPATI WONOSOBO,

Considering : a. that in order to improve the quality of public services in the field of licensing and non-licensing, it is necessary to establish procedures for granting permits and non-permit services in the Integrated Licensing Service Office;

b. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, it is necessary to establish a Bupati Regulation concerning Procedures for Granting Permits and Non-Permit Services in the Integrated Licensing Service Office;

In view of : 1. Law Number 13 of 1950 concerning the Formation of Autonomous Regions within Central Java Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1950 Number 42, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 9);

2. Law Number 8 of 1981 concerning Criminal Procedure Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1981 Number 76, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3209);

3. Law Number 28 of 1999 concerning State Administration that is Clean and Free from Corruption, Collusion and Nepotism (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 75, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3851);

4. Law Number 32 of 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 125, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4437) as amended several times, most recently by Law Number 12 of 2008 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 32 of 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2008 Number 59, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4844);

5. Law Number 25 of 2007 concerning Investment (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 67, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4724);

6. Law Number 25 of 2009 concerning Public Services (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2009 Number 112, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5038);

7. Government Regulation Number 27 of 1983 concerning Implementation of the Criminal Procedure Code (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1983 Number 36, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3258);

8. Government Regulation Number 38 of 2007 concerning Division of Government Affairs between the Government, Provincial Regional Governments, and Regency/City Regional Governments (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4737);

9. Presidential Regulation Number 27 of 2009 concerning Integrated One-Stop Services in the Investment Sector;

10. Minister of Home Affairs Regulation Number 24 of 2006 concerning Guidelines for the Implementation of Integrated One-Stop Services;

11. Minister of Home Affairs Regulation Number 20 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for the Organization and Work Procedures of Integrated Licensing Service Offices in Regions;

12. Wonosobo Regency Regional Regulation Number 11 of 2008 concerning the Organization and Work Procedures of Regional Agencies (Wonosobo Regency Regional Gazette of 2008 Number 11);

HAS DECIDED:

To establish : BUPATI REGULATION CONCERNING PROCEDURES FOR GRANTING PERMITS AND NON-PERMIT SERVICES IN THE INTEGRATED LICENSING SERVICE OFFICE.

CHAPTER I
GENERAL PROVISIONS

Article 1

In this Bupati Regulation, what is meant by:
1. Region is Wonosobo Regency.
2. Regional Government is the Bupati and Regional Apparatus as elements of regional government administration.
3. Bupati is the Bupati of Wonosobo.
4. Integrated Licensing Service Office, hereinafter abbreviated as KPPT, is a Regional Technical Implementation Unit that has the task of organizing the coordination and implementation of integrated one-stop services in the field of licensing and non-licensing.
5. Head of Office is the Head of the Integrated Licensing Service Office.
6. Permit is a permit that becomes the authority of the Wonosobo Regency Government.
7. Non-Permit is a service other than permits that becomes the authority of the Wonosobo Regency Government.
8. Applicant is an individual or legal entity that applies for a permit and/or non-permit.
9. Standard Operating Procedure, hereinafter abbreviated as SOP, is a guideline or reference for carrying out work tasks in accordance with the functions and performance assessment tools of government agencies based on technical, administrative and procedural indicators in accordance with work procedures, work flow and work procedures of the work unit concerned.
10. Technical Team is a team formed by the Bupati to provide technical considerations in the process of granting permits and non-permits.

CHAPTER II
SCOPE

Article 2

The scope of this Bupati Regulation includes:
a. types of permits and non-permits;
b. requirements and procedures for granting permits and non-permits;
c. processing time;
d. retribution rates;
e. rights and obligations;
f. supervision and control; and
g. sanctions.

CHAPTER III
TYPES OF PERMITS AND NON-PERMITS

Article 3

(1) Types of permits as referred to in Article 2 letter a consist of:
a. Nuisance Permit (HO);
b. Building Construction Permit (IMB);
c. Permit for Utilization of Groundwater (SIPA);
d. Trading Business License (SIUP);
e. Company Registration Certificate (TDP);
f. Industrial Business License (IUI);
g. Tourism Business License;
