PERMITS AND NON-PERMITS

Article 4

(1) Requirements and procedures for granting permits and non-permits as referred to in Article 2 letter b are regulated in the Standard Operating Procedure (SOP).

(2) Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) as referred to in paragraph (1) is established by the Bupati.

CHAPTER V
PROCESSING TIME

Article 5

(1) Processing time for permits and non-permits as referred to in Article 2 letter c is calculated from the date the application file is declared complete until the permit/non-permit is issued.

(2) Processing time for each type of permit and non-permit is regulated in the Standard Operating Procedure (SOP).

CHAPTER VI
RETRIBUTION RATES

Article 6

Retribution rates for permits and non-permits as referred to in Article 2 letter d are regulated in accordance with the provisions of applicable laws and regulations.

CHAPTER VII
RIGHTS AND OBLIGATIONS

Article 7

(1) Applicants have the right to:
a. obtain services in accordance with service standards;
b. obtain information regarding permit and non-permit requirements;
c. obtain certainty regarding processing time;
d. file complaints regarding services that do not comply with service standards.

(2) Applicants have the obligation to:
a. fulfill the requirements specified in the Standard Operating Procedure (SOP);
b. provide correct and accountable data/information;
c. pay retribution in accordance with applicable provisions;
d. comply with the provisions contained in the permit and/or non-permit issued.

Article 8

(1) KPPT has the right to:
a. request data/information from applicants;
b. reject applications that do not meet the requirements;
c. revoke permits that are not implemented in accordance with the provisions.

(2) KPPT has the obligation to:
a. provide services in accordance with service standards;
b. provide information regarding permit and non-permit requirements;
c. provide certainty regarding processing time;
d. maintain the confidentiality of applicant data/information.

CHAPTER VIII
SUPERVISION AND CONTROL

Article 9

(1) Supervision and control of the implementation of permits and non-permits is carried out by the Bupati.

(2) Supervision and control as referred to in paragraph (1) can be delegated to the Head of Office.

(3) Supervision and control as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out through:
a. monitoring and evaluation;
b. field inspection;
c. examination of reports.

CHAPTER IX
SANCTIONS

Article 10

(1) Permit holders who violate the provisions contained in the permit may be subject to administrative sanctions in the form of:
a. written warning;
b. temporary suspension of activities;
c. revocation of permit.

(2) Administrative sanctions as referred to in paragraph (1) are imposed by the Bupati or officials appointed by the Bupati.

CHAPTER X
TRANSITIONAL PROVISIONS

Article 11

Permits and non-permits that have been issued before the enactment of this Bupati Regulation remain valid until the expiration date.

CHAPTER XI
CLOSING PROVISIONS

Article 12

This Bupati Regulation comes into force on the date of promulgation.

In order that everyone may know of it, the promulgation of this Bupati Regulation is ordered by its placement in the Wonosobo Regency Gazette.

Enacted in Wonosobo
on December 30, 2011

BUPATI WONOSOBO,
Signed and sealed

